35.3.8 Orcish racial ascension - orc selected as the race, did
  not weild a non-orcish weapon (only orcish dagger, orcish short
  sword, orish spear, or orcish bow allowed), did not wear
  non-orcish armor (only orcish ring mail, orcish chain mail, orcish
  cloak, orcish helm, orcish shield or Uruk-hai shield allowed).
  Patience: Slight  Luck: Slight  Planning: Trivial

Orcie Notes

Orcs: Yes, there is some orcish armor (chainmail, cloak, helm,
shield). There is a good variety orcish weapons and even an
orcish artifact. However, that doesn't really make me want to
try an orc as a combat-wombat. First, while there is all of that
orcish stuff, none of it is particularly good. Second, orcs are
chaotic. Peruse the list of chaotic artifacts and you might notice
a certain gap. There is no chaotic artifact that offers magic
resistance. MR is a rather nice atribute to have. Given that
I want to avoid any non-orcish armor (thus no cloak of magic
resistance or gray dragon scale(s)(mail)) the only way to get
MR is from an artifact. Well, what artifact that grants MR is
accessible? The Eye of the Aethiopica. Orcs can be wizards, so
that seems to be the way to go.

Note that the armor class for this character will still be pretty
bad. Sure, I'll have an orcish cloak loaded up, and possibly a
shield (I'll have to see how much that increases the spell
failure rate), but we are still looking at an armor class of
what? -13 or so? Rather different than a unrestricted character
that can hit something in the negative forties.

